  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catholic Institute for International Relations (CIIR) - Consolidated Grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Minimising the effects of poverty and injustice through education and sharing of skills in the south.
Securing policy reforms which will benefit populations in developing countries.
CIIR has geographically focussed programmes with advocacy coordinators  attached to specific regional teams, but each covering the broad themes of civil society and participatory development , justice and human security, and international economics and poverty.
CIIR is committed to working closely with sister organisations in the North and South, and to developing policy through discussion and compromise, ensuring that everyone&apos;s views are taken into account. 
The themes and priorities identified in CIIR&apos;s strategic framework for 2005-2010 are: Civil Society Participation; HIV and AIDS; and Sustainable Environment.</narrative>
  </description>
